CLASS MedalUnlockQueue
    DESCRIPTION: Durable buffer of medal unlocks that were requested but never confirmed, plus the background pass that retries them
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    NOTE: This is a hand-written class that does NOT extend BaseObject

    PURPOSE: A medal unlock is a single request, and a request can go missing. The connection
    drops partway through, the server is down, or the player closes the tab before the response
    comes back. In every one of those cases the player has already earned the medal.

    WHY NOT AN IN-MEMORY QUEUE?: The thing that lost the request is usually the same thing that
    ended the page. So ids are written to STORAGE before the request goes out, and cleared only
    once the gateway has actually ruled on them.

    OWNERSHIP: Core creates one of these in its constructor, the same way it creates AppState.
    That is what scopes the buffer correctly: the pending set belongs to one App ID, and Core is
    the per-app instance, so a static singleton would be wrong the moment two Cores run for two
    different projects.

    CADENCE: NGIO owns the retry timer and nothing else, exactly as it does for keepAlive(): it
    holds the timer, and the work happens down here. See NGIO.retryPendingMedalUnlocks() and
    NGIO.startMedalUnlockRetryTimer().

    DEPENDENCIES: The generated models, Errors, and Core (which it uses to send each unlock).

    ====================
    PROPERTIES
    ====================

    PRIVATE core: Core
        PURPOSE: The Core instance this queue belongs to
        WHY: Used to send each Medal.unlock, and to scope the storage key by App ID

    PRIVATE storageKey: String
        PURPOSE: A unique key used to avoid naming collisions when saving the pending id list
        WHY: Storage keys MUST contain the App ID. Apps hosted on the same host share a storage
        space, so an unqualified key collides across every game using this library there. Same
        reasoning as AppState.sessionStorageKey.
        DEFAULT: "ngio-pending-medal-unlocks-for-" + core.appId

    PRIVATE inFlight: Set of Integer
        PURPOSE: The ids currently out on a live request, foreground or retry
        WHY: Lets a background pass skip anything already being sent instead of firing a
        duplicate request for the same id
        DEFAULT: Empty
        NOTE: In memory only. This describes right now, not something that has to survive a
        reload, so unlike the pending list it is deliberately NOT persisted.

    ====================
    CONSTRUCTOR
    ====================

    FUNCTION constructor(core: Core)
        PARAMETERS:
            core: (required) The Core instance that owns this queue

        BEHAVIOR:
            SET this.core TO core
            SET this.storageKey TO "ngio-pending-medal-unlocks-for-" + core.appId
            SET this.inFlight TO an empty set
    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    PUBLIC METHODS
    ====================

    FUNCTION getPendingIds(): Array of Integer
        PURPOSE: Lists the medal ids currently recorded as requested but not yet ruled on

        RETURNS: An array or list of medal ids, empty when nothing is pending

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CREATE raw AS STORAGE_GET(this.storageKey)
                IF raw is null OR raw is empty THEN
                    RETURN an empty list
                END IF

                CREATE parsed AS JSON_DECODE(raw)
                IF parsed is not a list THEN
                    RETURN an empty list
                END IF

                RETURN only the entries of parsed that are numbers
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Unparseable stored data is treated as ABSENT, not fatal. Corrupt local
                COMMENT: state must degrade to "nothing pending", never crash an unlock.
                RETURN an empty list
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION unlock(ids: Array of Integer, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Unlocks one or more medals, recording each id before it is sent

        PARAMETERS:
            ids: (required) The medal ids to unlock
            callback: Function to call once every id has come back, as callback(outcomes)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback

        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            outcomes: One entry per id, each holding id, the unlocked medal (or null), and an
                      error (or null). The error is the only reliable success signal.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE unique AS ids with duplicates removed
            IF unique is empty THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING an empty list
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: Record every id as pending BEFORE sending anything. It might look as
            COMMENT: though a medal that fails against a healthy gateway should never have been
            COMMENT: buffered at all - do NOT restructure it that way. Writing before the send
            COMMENT: is what makes a crash or reload mid-request survivable. An id that fails
            COMMENT: against a healthy gateway sits here for a few milliseconds, costing nothing.
            CALL this.addPending(unique)

            CREATE outcomes AS an empty list
            CREATE remaining AS the length of unique

            FOR EACH id IN unique
                ADD id TO this.inFlight

                COMMENT: One request per medal, NOT one batch. The gateway rules on each medal
                COMMENT: separately, and Core's component queue is shared with the game, so a
                COMMENT: background pass must never drain it.
                CALL this.core.callComponent("Medal.unlock", { id: id }, FUNCTION onComplete(response)
                    REMOVE id FROM this.inFlight

                    CREATE outcome AS this.adjudicate(id, response)
                    IF outcome.adjudicated is true THEN
                        COMMENT: The gateway ruled on this medal. Its fate is settled and
                        COMMENT: retrying cannot change it, so drop it whether the answer was
                        COMMENT: yes or no.
                        CALL this.removePending(id)
                    END IF

                    ADD { id: id, medal: outcome.medal, error: outcome.error } TO outcomes
                    SET remaining TO remaining - 1
                    IF remaining is 0 AND callback is defined THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING outcomes
                    END IF
                END FUNCTION, this)
            END FOR

        NOTE: A fresh unlock ALWAYS sends immediately. Nothing here waits on the retry pass.
        The background pass exists only to recover requests an earlier attempt never got
        confirmation for.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION retryPending()
        PURPOSE: Re-sends everything still in the pending list

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CREATE pending AS this.getPendingIds() minus anything in this.inFlight
                IF pending is empty THEN
                    RETURN
                END IF
                CALL this.unlock(pending, null, null)
            CATCH
                COMMENT: This NEVER throws and never reports a failure. A pass that cannot reach
                COMMENT: the gateway is exactly the case it exists to tolerate, and one bad pass
                COMMENT: must not stop later ones from running.
            END TRY

        NOTE: Safe to call by hand, for instance on an application-level "back online" event.
    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    PRIVATE METHODS
    ====================

    FUNCTION adjudicate(id: Integer, response: Response): Object
        PURPOSE: Decides whether the gateway actually ruled on this specific medal

        RETURNS: An object holding id, medal, error, and adjudicated

        WHY: The buffer exists to survive connectivity failures, and NOTHING else. So the
        question to ask of every outcome is not "did this succeed?" but "has the gateway ruled
        on this specific medal?" If it has, retrying cannot change the answer.

        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT: What came back                              | Ruled on? | Action
        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT: No response at all                          | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A response, but success is not true         | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A per-medal result that succeeded           | Yes       | DROP
        COMMENT: A per-medal failure on 102/104/110/111      | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A per-medal failure on anything else (202)  | Yes       | DROP
        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Nothing reached the gateway, or nothing came back.
            IF response is null OR response has no getResult method THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: an error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            COMMENT: The envelope was rejected before this medal was considered.
            IF response.success is not true THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: response.error OR an error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            CREATE result AS response.getResult()
            IF result is null THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: an "invalid response" error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            IF result.success is true THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: result.medal, error: null, adjudicated: true }
            END IF

            CREATE error AS result.error OR an "invalid response" error
            CREATE code AS error.code

            COMMENT: Session-class codes mean the call was blocked on identity before the medal
            COMMENT: was looked at, so it is NOT adjudicated.
            IF code is 102 OR code is 104 OR code is 110 OR code is 111 THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            COMMENT: Anything else means the gateway looked at this medal and rejected it, 202
            COMMENT: (INVALID_MEDAL_ID) above all. A medal id that no longer exists, or was
            COMMENT: mistyped, or was removed from the game is dropped on the first response
            COMMENT: that reaches the gateway and never retries again.
            RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: error, adjudicated: true }

        NOTE: The session-class row is NOT an exception to the rule. Medal.unlock requires a
        login, so an unlock attempted while signed out is refused LOCALLY by
        BaseComponent.getPreflightError() and never sent, with code 102 or 110. That refusal is
        deliberately built to be indistinguishable from a server refusal, so you cannot tell
        where it came from. You do not need to: discriminating on the error CLASS puts the local
        refusal in the keep set for free, which is the right outcome. A player who earns a medal
        as a guest and signs in later should still get it.

        NOTE: With this rule there is no retry cap, no attempt counter, and no maximum age, and
        none of them are needed. Nothing can retry indefinitely except a genuine connectivity
        failure, which is exactly what should.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION addPending(ids: Array of Integer)
        PURPOSE: Adds ids to the stored pending list

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE current AS the set of this.getPendingIds()
            ADD every id in ids TO current
            CALL this.write(current)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION removePending(id: Integer)
        PURPOSE: Drops one id from the stored pending list

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE current AS the set of this.getPendingIds()
            IF id is not in current THEN
                RETURN
            END IF
            REMOVE id FROM current
            CALL this.write(current)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION write(ids: Set of Integer)
        PURPOSE: Persists the pending list

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CALL STORAGE_SET(this.storageKey, JSON_ENCODE(ids as a list))
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Best-effort durability, never fatal. Quota limits, private browsing,
                COMMENT: and storage disabled by the user are all real, and none of them should
                COMMENT: turn an unlock into an error.
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS
